WEBVTT

welcome-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.769
Hi Sophie.

welcome-2
00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:04.231
This short video explains your mortgage offer from Fernmoor.

welcome-3
00:00:04.231 --> 00:00:06.154
It takes about two minutes.

welcome-4
00:00:06.154 --> 00:00:11.154
You can pause, turn on captions, or ask a question at any time.

your-loan-1
00:00:11.154 --> 00:00:14.615
You're borrowing £297,500 to buy a home worth £350,000.

your-loan-2
00:00:14.615 --> 00:00:16.923
That's 85 percent of its value.

your-loan-3
00:00:16.923 --> 00:00:19.615
Lenders call this your loan to value.

your-loan-4
00:00:19.615 --> 00:00:22.308
You'll pay it back over 35 years.

your-rate-1
00:00:22.308 --> 00:00:26.923
For the first 2 years, your rate is fixed at 5.09 percent.

your-rate-2
00:00:26.923 --> 00:00:31.154
Your monthly payment stays at £1,518.57, even if interest rates change.

after-fixed-1
00:00:31.154 --> 00:00:34.231
Your fixed rate ends on 30 November 2028.

after-fixed-2
00:00:34.231 --> 00:00:37.692
After that, you move to our Standard Variable Rate.

after-fixed-3
00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:41.923
It's 7.49 percent today, and it can go up or down.

after-fixed-4
00:00:41.923 --> 00:00:46.923
If it stays the same, your payment would rise to £1,985.46 a month.

after-fixed-5
00:00:46.923 --> 00:00:48.077
That's £466.89 more.

after-fixed-6
00:00:48.077 --> 00:00:52.308
Many people choose a new deal before their fixed rate ends.

overpayments-1
00:00:52.308 --> 00:00:59.231
You can pay off up to 10 percent of what you owe each year at no extra cost.

overpayments-2
00:00:59.231 --> 00:01:05.000
If you repay more than that during your fixed rate, there's an early repayment charge.

overpayments-3
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.615
It's 3 percent in year 1 and 2 percent in year 2.

overpayments-4
00:01:09.615 --> 00:01:15.000
For example, repaying an extra ten thousand pounds in year 1 would cost £300.

fees-1
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.308
There's a product fee of £1,499.00.

fees-2
00:01:17.308 --> 00:01:20.000
You pay it when your mortgage completes.

fees-3
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.308
It isn't added to your loan.

total-cost-1
00:01:22.308 --> 00:01:28.077
Over the full 35 years, you'd repay about £824,186 in total, if rates don't change.

total-cost-2
00:01:28.077 --> 00:01:32.308
That includes your loan of £297,500 and the interest on it.

your-part-1
00:01:32.308 --> 00:01:35.769
There are a few things you need to do.

your-part-2
00:01:35.769 --> 00:01:37.308
Keep up your payments.

your-part-3
00:01:37.308 --> 00:01:40.385
Your home may be repossessed if you don't.

your-part-4
00:01:40.385 --> 00:01:41.923
Keep your home insured.

your-part-5
00:01:41.923 --> 00:01:45.769
And remember, this offer is valid until 1 April 2027.

contact-1
00:01:45.769 --> 00:01:51.154
If anything isn't clear, type a question in the box next to this video.

contact-2
00:01:51.154 --> 00:01:55.000
Or call us on 01632 960412 and quote your reference.

contact-3
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.538
Thanks for watching, Sophie.
